00747796919,"_gp_mult_vs_hist":false,"_score_mult_vs_hist":67.5,"_gate_fcf_yield":0.04461092321277681,"_gp_fcf_yield":false,"_score_fcf_yield":21.0,"_gate_int_coverage":25.277511512075932,"_gp_int_coverage":true,"_score_int_coverage":100.0,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":0.20294829337085998,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":84.4,"_gate_accruals":-0.047206700319124044,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":59.1,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.11154382791946571,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":82.4,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.013377852890387065,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":83.3,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.07356776341440967,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":36.8,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.18320123268240243,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":69.5,"_gate_incr_roic":0.167192477953203,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":72.4,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.03752514362008472,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":45.8,"_gate_pool_share":0.02909468998193665,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":51.6,"_gate_rev_durability":0.08705841356203092,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":68.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.004761890603594665,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":27.4,"_gate_margins":0.0032598484292219675,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":53.3,"_gate_fund_growth":0.0525481781997869,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":52.5,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.048474079200635393,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":65.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.010151757333531686,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":62.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0061916715542522,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":89.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.07285,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":48.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Franklin Electric Co., Inc., together with its subsidiaries, designs, manufactures, and distributes water and fuel pumping systems in the United States, Canada, Latin America, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific. It operates through Water Systems, Energy Systems, and Distribution segments. The Water Systems segment offers motors, pumps, water treatment systems, monitoring devices, and related parts and equipment for use in groundwater, water transfer, and wastewater in a range of residential, agricultural, municipal, and industrial applications; and electronic drives and controls for the motors, which control functionality and provide protection from various hazards, such as electrical surges, over-heating, and dry wells or dry tanks. Its Energy Systems segment produces and markets pumps, motors, pipes, sumps, fittings, vapor recovery components, electronic controls, monitoring devices, and related parts and equipment for use in energy system applications; and components between the tanks and the dispensers, including submersible pumps, station hardware, piping, and corrosion control systems. This segment serves other energy markets, such as power reliability systems, including intelligent electronic devices that are designed for online monitoring for the power utility, hydroelectric, rail, and telecommunication and data center infrastructure. The Distribution segment sells to and provides presale support and specifications to the installing contractors. In addition, the company manufactures precision triplex reciprocating pumps and systems. It sells its products to wholesale and retail distributors, specialty distributors, and industrial and petroleum equipment distributors, as well as to oil and utility companies, and original equipment manufacturers. The company was founded in 1944 and is headquartered in Fort Wayne, Indiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joseph A. Ruzynski | CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $328K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $30K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Franklin Electric Co., Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $4.3B market cap on $2.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 9% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 34%.","The business throws off $194M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.62\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 25\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 4.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 7.3% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 17% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","33 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Franklin Electric (FELE) Upgraded to Strong Buy: Here's What You Should Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028915/franklin-electric-fele-upgraded-to-strong-buy-here-s-what-you-should-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_12_zacks_rank_upgrade-3028915","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794499203.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Discipline and Rules-Based Execution in FELE Response","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/10/Discipline_and_Rules-Based_Execution_in_FELE_Response_111126050402_1794391442.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794391442.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Raised Outlook Could Be A Game Changer For Franklin Electric Stock (FELE)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-fele/franklin-electric/news/raised-outlook-could-be-a-game-changer-for-franklin-electric","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794364816.954,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Franklin Electric (FELE) Lifts Revenue Outlook, Is It Still 24% Undervalued?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-fel